  "question": {
    "text": "A series combination of resistor of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;inductor of inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math> is connected to an ac source. The quality factor of the circuit will be _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the quality factor of an LCR circuit is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (1) to calculate the required quality factor of the circuit.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>Q</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
